TITLE:: REScoreVisuals
summary:: The visuals feed of a score: what is recorded and what replays, to HomewareVisuals
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/REScoreRecorder, Classes/REScorePlayer, Classes/RCVisuals

DESCRIPTION::
Sends what a song's link::Classes/REScoreRecorder:: records and what an link::Classes/REScorePlayer:: plays to HomewareVisuals through link::Classes/RCVisuals:: (OSC 57121, the bridge, a page), so that a page draws the performance's score as it is made and as it replays (HomewareVisuals' code::public/lib/score-viz.js::, the page code::public/score/::). The protocol is the header of the class file: one JSON string per message under code::/score:: (code::take::, code::events::, code::event::, code::played::, code::head::, code::stop::, code::stopPlay::). It chains the recorder's and the player's hooks (their own keep running) and records nothing.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: recorder
An REScoreRecorder to attach to (nil: none yet).
argument:: player
An REScorePlayer to attach to (nil: none yet).

METHOD:: prefix
The paths' prefix, code::/score::.
METHOD:: chunk
Events per code::/score/events:: message (40: an OSC packet stays under 64 kB).
METHOD:: headRate
Head messages per second (10).
METHOD:: textLength
Characters of a code line kept in an event message (80).

METHOD:: eventDict
A compact event for the page: id, beat, secs, kind, level, voice, cause, the control key as words and the value it sets, the names, a code line's first characters.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: attach
Attach to a recorder: a take's start, every event, the recording head, the stop.
METHOD:: attachPlayer
Attach to a player: the take it plays (its events in chunks), every event fired, the playhead, the stop.
METHOD:: detach
METHOD:: detachRecorder
METHOD:: detachPlayer
The hooks put back as they were.
METHOD:: recorder
METHOD:: player
METHOD:: name
The name of the take being fed.
METHOD:: send
A message under the prefix, its dictionary as JSON (Symbols as plain strings).

EXAMPLES::

code::
~viz = REScoreVisuals(~song.scoreRecorder);
~rec.record([4, 0]);              // the page sees the take grow
~rec.stop;
~p = REScorePlayer(REScore.read(path), ~song);
~viz.attachPlayer(~p);
~p.play([4, 0]);                  // the page draws the take and follows the playhead
~viz.detach;
::
